WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:05.580
A mysterious story of survival, betrayal,
and desperation, Yellowjackets was an instant

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:08.610
hit — but what should we know going into
Season 2?

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:14.360
Season 1 of Yellowjackets premiered in November
2021, and chronicled the events of a devastating

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:18.660
plane crash that left the members of a women's
high school soccer team stranded in the woods

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:21.810
without contact or rescue for 19 months.

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:25.850
Depicting the twin storylines of the time
immediately after the crash and the lives

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:31.234
of the tragedy's few survivors a few decades
later, the show was quickly met with critical acclaim,

00:00:31.234 --> 00:00:35.190
For those who watched the show around the
time that it aired, your long wait for a follow

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:39.160
up to Season 1's intense cliffhangers will
come to an end shortly.

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:43.730
Yellowjackets Season 2 will premiere on streaming
and on-demand for Showtime subscribers on

00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:47.850
March 24, and will premiere on air on March
26.

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:52.180
While a long year may have passed since the
finale premiered, the time fans have had to

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:56.350
wait just means they can expect Season 2 to
be the best it can possibly be.

00:00:56.350 --> 00:00:58.190
Showrunner Ashley Lyle told TheWrap,

00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:02.510
"It's a deeply serialized story and we wanted
to make sure we didn't rush it, and that we

00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:03.510
got it right.

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:05.820
And so this was the earliest we could accomplish
that."

00:01:06.194 --> 00:01:10.940
As the first season of "Yellowjackets" comes
to a conclusion, we flash back to the '90s

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:15.330
and see that the teens are about to face down
a frigid winter in a Canadian forest.

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:19.920
Jealousy, hunger, and madness are beginning
to set in, and we know for a fact that Season

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:22.633
2 will focus on this dark and dangerous period.

00:01:22.633 --> 00:01:24.940
"None of this would have happened if it wasn't
for you.

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:25.609
If you hadn't—"

00:01:25.609 --> 00:01:26.856
"What?

00:01:27.817 --> 00:01:29.457
Huh?

00:01:29.632 --> 00:01:30.632
Stolen him?"

00:01:30.850 --> 00:01:34.810
Speaking with Variety, showrunner Ashley Lyle
confirmed the show would be returning to the

00:01:34.810 --> 00:01:35.810
cold forest.

00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:40.510
During this storyline, viewers will likely
learn about the forces stalking our protagonists,

00:01:40.510 --> 00:01:44.759
why the forest refuses to let them leave,
and how low and desperate the behavior of

00:01:44.759 --> 00:01:47.840
the freezing teammates becomes as the days
grow shorter.

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:51.420
As for the present-day timeline, we're not
exactly sure where the show will go from there,

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:55.549
but it will no doubt involve the murder of
Adam Martin, the kidnapping of Natalie, and

00:01:55.549 --> 00:01:57.098
the return of Lottie.

00:01:57.369 --> 00:02:02.060
One of the strongest aspects of Yellowjackets
is its incredibly talented cast.

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:04.040
But who will be coming back for Season 2?

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:08.780
Well, we know that Melanie Lynskey, Christina
Ricci, Juliette Lewis, and Tawny Cypress are

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:13.280
returning to play the adult versions of Shauna,
Misty, Natalie, and Taissa.

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:18.310
Plus, Sophie Nélisse, Samantha Hanratty,
Sophie Thatcher, and Jasmin Savoy Brown are

00:02:18.310 --> 00:02:21.420
all coming back to play their respective teenage
counterparts.

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:26.830
We can also expect to see Liv Hewson as teenage
Van and Courtney Eaton as young Lottie — both

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:28.840
of whom have been made series regulars.

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:33.390
However, the big question remains: will we
see their adult versions?

00:02:33.390 --> 00:02:35.730
As it turns out, the answer is yes.

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:40.530
Lauren Ambrose of Servant and Six Feet Under
will play the adult version of Van while Simone

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:45.430
Kessell of Our Flag Means Death and Obi-Wan
Kenobi will be starring as the Antler Queen

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:47.060
herself — Lottie.

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:50.760
Kevin Alves will also be returning to play
series regular Travis.

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:54.720
You may also want to keep an eye out for Lynskey's
real-life husband, Jason Ritter.

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:59.890
Also, Nia Sondaya of Truth Be Told has been
cast as teen Akilah, replacing Keeya King.

00:02:59.890 --> 00:03:04.980
Variety reports that Nicole Maines of Supergirl
and François Arnaud of The Borgias have also

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:06.060
joined the cast.

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:09.920
Maines will be playing Lisa, someone with
a connection to the adult version of Lottie,

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:12.349
while Arnaud will play Coach Scott's boyfriend.

00:03:12.349 --> 00:03:15.650
"Did you hear that mom?

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:16.257
Dad?

00:03:16.257 --> 00:03:17.257
God?

00:03:17.752 --> 00:03:20.220
All my furry forest friends?

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:21.730
I'm gay!"

00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:26.500
Other small roles we'll be seeing again include
Steven Krueger as Coach Ben Scott and Warren

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:28.130
Kole as Shauna's husband.

00:03:28.130 --> 00:03:32.110
However, perhaps the biggest casting news
comes straight from Middle-earth.

00:03:32.110 --> 00:03:36.780
According to Deadline, Elijah Wood has signed
on for a season-long guest arc as a citizen

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:38.758
detective alongside Misty.

00:03:39.201 --> 00:03:43.230
The folks at Showtime seem to have taken a
"if it ain't broke, don't fix it" approach

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:48.200
to Yellowjackets Season 2 by bringing back
the warped geniuses behind the first season.

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:53.299
Ashley Lyle and Bart Nickerson make up the
dynamic duo who created the visceral survival

00:03:53.299 --> 00:03:57.480
series, and — along with Jonathan Lisco
— they were the creatives running the show.

00:03:57.480 --> 00:04:01.740
Needless to say, their twisted brainchild
became a smash hit, earning all three Emmy

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:04.959
nominations and a place on Season 2's production
team.

00:04:04.959 --> 00:04:09.530
In fact, Showtime was so impressed with Lyle
and Nickerson that the company signed them

00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:12.950
to an overall deal, allowing them to work
on new Showtime series.

00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:16.919
While we're excited to see what new messed-up
projects they'll cook up, we're mostly psyched

00:04:16.919 --> 00:04:21.090
to see the original showrunners bring "Yellowjackets"
Season 2 to horrifying life.

00:04:21.734 --> 00:04:26.410
Similar to most TV series, the individual
episodes of Yellowjackets Season 1 were helmed

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:27.919
by different directors.

00:04:27.919 --> 00:04:32.460
Some standouts to work on the first season
include feature directors Eduardo Sánchez

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:37.180
and Daisy von Scherler Mayer, as well Billie
Woodruff, who's worked on numerous music videos

00:04:37.180 --> 00:04:38.900
with Joe and Toni Braxton.

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:43.970
However, perhaps the biggest get for the show
was Karyn Kusama, who directed the pilot and

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:46.509
served as an executive producer for the series.

00:04:46.509 --> 00:04:51.169
Kusama excels in tense films that play with
horrific concepts like The Invitation and

00:04:51.169 --> 00:04:52.389
Jennifer's Body.

00:04:52.389 --> 00:04:56.590
And that suspenseful expertise is on full
display in the pilot episode, which opens

00:04:56.590 --> 00:05:01.460
with a terrifying sequence where a young girl
runs for her life, hunted by her former teammates.

00:05:01.460 --> 00:05:06.199
It's a gut-punch of a first episode, and fortunately,
Kusama is coming back for Season 2.

00:05:06.199 --> 00:05:08.259
Speaking about the new season, she told The
Playlist

00:05:08.259 --> 00:05:13.110
"Season 1, in my opinion, did a great job
of completely upending the idea of an expected

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:14.550
direction for any of it.

00:05:14.550 --> 00:05:18.199
And so I would just say that Season 2 is a
continuation of that kind of surprise and

00:05:18.199 --> 00:05:22.693
humor and tonal collision that is essentially
as surprising and crazy as real life."

00:05:23.084 --> 00:05:27.590
There's a whole lot going on in Yellowjackets
Season 1, from Shauna's pregnancy to Lottie's

00:05:27.590 --> 00:05:31.350
cult to the seemingly supernatural forces
lurking in the forest.

00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:36.000
And with two timelines to follow, you'll no
doubt need a refresher before Season 2 is released.

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:38.940
So where can you catch up on all the survivalist
horror?

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:42.970
Well, if you want to revisit "Yellowjackets"
Season 1 check it out for the first time,

00:05:42.970 --> 00:05:46.660
you can do so by visiting Showtime, where
you can watch the series for the cost of a

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:47.949
monthly subscription.

